# Causey UI

Before new UI: reuse an existing pattern in this repo. If none fits, follow tokens below — do not invent a variant "because it looks modern."

Every screen must be easy to read and intuitive to use on first view: clear type hierarchy, plain-language labels, one obvious next action. If a layout needs explaining, it is wrong.

Causey is a scholastic competition product for club coaches, district program offices, and students. Alive means density, thicker type, rounder controls, and one coordinated motion system — not empty cards and not a toy palette.

## Brand
- Fonts: Source Sans 3 (UI/body, default weight 500), Source Serif 4 (`font-display` for headlines/wordmark, weight 800). Never Inter/Roboto/system-as-brand.
- Colors: only CSS tokens (`brand-red`, `brand-blue`, `surface`, `muted`, etc.). Red = primary action; blue = secondary/calm. Never equal-weight red+blue CTAs.
- Radius: controls `rounded-xl`, cards `rounded-2xl`, hero shells `rounded-3xl`. No `rounded-full` status pills.
- Banned looks: purple/indigo gradients, cream+terracotta AI default, broadsheet newspaper gimmick, dark mode by default, glow/glass/neon shadows.

## Layout & components
- One job per section; one dominant CTA per view.
- The first viewport is full of the product object (search, roster, path), not padding around a headline.
- Filled panels, not bubbles with air: any card/panel/band must be composed so its content fills it — no large dead blank areas, and no lopsided two-column layouts where one side runs long while the other sits empty. Rebalance (move or trim content, cap the long column, stack earlier) or cut the container.
- If a card has fewer than about four content rows, it is a list row or a left-rule strip, not a bordered bubble.
- Marketing band padding-block: 2–2.5rem default, 3rem max unless the viewport is filled with a product object.
- Same rule at page scale: no dead blank zones anywhere on a page. A page with a composed panel on one side and an empty expanse on the other was not planned. Plan the whole canvas — fill it, rebalance it, or narrow the layout — so pages ship right the first time instead of needing redesign passes later.
- Cards for interaction, repeating units, or discrete chunks that benefit from separation. Bento/feature grids OK when content is genuinely grid-shaped — no identical pastel icon cells.
- No `rounded-full` status pills above heroes. Badges must be functional (real filter/status/category) or deleted.
- Results layout toggle: desktop (`lg+`) only — mobile stays single column.
- Chess hero graphic: tune via `CHESS_GRAPHIC_SCALE` in `ChessHeroGraphic.tsx`; hidden on phones, shown md+.

## Dual-buyer surfaces
- District chrome: School/District copy, dense tables, calm path/progress motion.
- Club/student chrome: Club/Team copy, same tokens, tighter packing, athletic cues (date chips, roster density).
- Do not invent a second palette.

## Copy
- Direct, specific, student-access focused. Headlines must say something only Causey can say.
- Avoid em-dash spam and banned filler alone: "New", "Beta", "Coming soon", "AI-powered", "Live", "Pre-launch".
- No fake data, no ✨, no placeholder lorem. Empty/error states say what to do next.

## Motion
- Motion is required as ONE coordinated system per page: hero entrance, a single shared scroll-reveal pattern, progress/draw moments, short staggers on small groups.
- Marketing pages and role landings fail review without a signature moment.
- Ambient motion only on the coordinate-grid `::before` layer. Text, nav, buttons, and fields stay still at rest.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (non-negotiable).

